# Normalize line endings to LF on checkout across every platform. block hashes
# committed files and compares the digest against a recorded one: registry/ is a
# vendored copy of block-registry, and registry/SNAPSHOT holds the sha256 of the
# recipes as they were vendored. On Windows CI, git's autocrlf would otherwise
# check those .toml files out with CRLF, so every byte-for-byte comparison —
# the snapshot check, the golden files under e2e/ — would differ from the digest
# recorded on Linux. Forcing eol=lf keeps the comparison deterministic on Linux,
# macOS, and Windows alike.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be EOL-translated (it would corrupt them).
*.png -text
*.gif -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.ico -text
*.bin -text
*.pdf -text
*.gz -text
*.zip -text
